WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.025
Here's who reads those tags
once a server is connected.

2
00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:05.896
Machine configuration,
from the last chapter,

3
00:00:05.896 --> 00:00:09.975
only enforces on servers whose
configuration owner tag names it.

4
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:15.012
Update Manager's dynamic scopes can group
machines by tag, and they're evaluated

5
00:00:15.012 --> 00:00:19.438
at every scheduled run, so a scope on
the patch owner tag follows the tag.

6
00:00:19.438 --> 00:00:22.876
The built-in assessment policy
can be scoped by tag too.

7
00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:25.207
And the validation kit
checks afterward for

8
00:00:25.207 --> 00:00:27.475
a server carrying
enforcement it shouldn't.

9
00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:30.988
Every one of them depends on the
tag being right from the start.

10
00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:32.540
Next, which Azure.
